WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.290
- This is huge!

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.160
Sorry, I'm just.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.530
- You look great, it's been a long time.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.280
- Holy schmoly.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.021
- That's right, holy shmoly, that's right.

00:00:08.021 --> 00:00:10.300
That would be the TV
version of the phrase.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.550
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.999
- We first met on December 10th, 1991.

00:00:15.999 --> 00:00:17.320
You were what, 10 or 11?

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.430
- I think I had just turned 11.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.263
- [Jay] Yeah, that's right.

00:00:21.263 --> 00:00:22.230
- Yeah, I had just turned 11.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.501
And yeah, seeing you today,
yeah, it's bringing back a lot.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.334
(Anna laughing)

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:28.167
- Now, I remember back then,

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.350
you said you wanted to
be a paleontologist.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.120
A very serious young woman, yeah.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.220
I'm going to be a paleontologist.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.480
- Yeah, yeah, I did.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.544
- How'd that work out?

00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:39.120
(Anna laughing)

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.340
- I haven't even played a paleontologist.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.640
So, I suppose I still have
some dreams to come true.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.080
- Now, you have kids of your own now.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:46.913
- I do.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.990
- Okay, now, I read something.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.390
They're fascinated by seeing you cry?

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.980
As an actress, you mean,
is that what it is?

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.290
- No, they haven't seen my work yet.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.880
Yeah, a lot of the work I do

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.380
is not
- Not for kids.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.220
- Suitable for children.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.053
- Okay,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.010
No, it's not porn.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:02.879
Please, could we.
- Yeah, it's not creepy.

00:01:02.879 --> 00:01:03.712
Like, chill out.

00:01:03.712 --> 00:01:04.620
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:06.123
- It just came off bad.

00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:08.887
(Anna laughing)

00:01:08.887 --> 00:01:09.930
- Yeah.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:12.087
- Yeah, no, it's just, you know.

00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:13.807
Grownup themes.
- No, it's adult themes.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:14.640
Grownup themes.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.706
- Yeah, but, you know, they like to see

00:01:17.706 --> 00:01:21.780
when I definitely will cry at a movie.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:22.613
- [Jay] Right.

00:01:22.613 --> 00:01:24.063
- And, usually, there are certain movies.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.360
What comes to mind is there's
a certain song in Mulana

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.430
and there's a certain
sequence in Inside Out

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:32.280
where, basically, if I
just hear the music, I'll.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.113
- [Jay] Really?

00:01:33.113 --> 00:01:34.800
- I'll just, it's Pavlovian at this point.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:35.998
- Right.

00:01:35.998 --> 00:01:38.013
Now, is it just cartoons you cry at, or?

00:01:39.297 --> 00:01:40.173
- Yeah, I mean.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.520
I suppose I've definitely
cried at Sound of Music.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.720
I've cried at, I cry in
movies, I cry watching movies.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.840
But they get very excited to, like,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.140
to kind of confirm their
suspicion that this will happen.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:55.973
You know?
- Really?

00:01:55.973 --> 00:01:57.240
- I'm like a scientific
experiment at that point.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.190
- You see, I would cry, like,

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.920
when a car crashes in Fast and
Furious, because I like cars.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.390
- Because you like cars!

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.410
- Look at that Chevy!

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:05.883
- No, it's true.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:08.367
It's true.
- Chevy's.

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:10.680
- And those cars appreciate your love.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.513
- That's right, that's right.

00:02:11.513 --> 00:02:12.381
- Yes.

00:02:12.381 --> 00:02:13.214
(Anna laughing)

00:02:13.214 --> 00:02:16.170
- So, do your kids
understand joking and lying,

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.643
and fake crying and?

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.880
- I mean, this is something
that I think still,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.050
I mean, this is what I tell my kids too,

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:23.640
I'm like grownups are
still trying to figure out

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.780
the difference between lying
and joking and honesty.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.954
- Between lying and joking?

00:02:28.954 --> 00:02:31.980
- Yeah, my eldest daughter
asked me that one day.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.180
She was like, mom, what's the difference

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.490
between a lie and a joke?

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:39.000
And I really had to think
about it, because I don't like

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.317
dishonesty in my own life.
- Right, sure.

00:02:40.317 --> 00:02:41.370
- I'm not cool with it.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.970
And, so, I really wanted
to make sense of that.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.890
But I have to make sense
of that for myself first,

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:48.870
before I tell her.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:53.160
So, I don't know, I was like,
lying, when somebody lies,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.500
they don't intend to tell you the truth.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.750
And that's not fair, right?

00:02:57.750 --> 00:02:59.790
Somebody doesn't get to know
the truth when you don't.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.540
- You see, my favorite are
kids doing that kind of thing.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.830
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.330
- You know, I had a kid
write me a letter once.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.500
He said, dear Mr. Leno, he was about 12.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.570
He said, I told my friends you're my uncle

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:16.410
and on Sundays we go for
rides in your Lamborghini.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:17.670
And he goes on to this whole thing.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:18.503
- What?

00:03:18.503 --> 00:03:21.060
- He said, could you
pick me up at my house.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:21.893
- [Anna] Poppy!

00:03:21.893 --> 00:03:22.830
- And give me a ride to school,

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.750
so my friends won't know I'm a liar.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.317
- Oh, but you are.

00:03:26.317 --> 00:03:28.805
- I said, but you are, you are a liar!

00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:29.638
And you are a liar!

00:03:29.638 --> 00:03:30.471
(Anna laughing)

00:03:30.471 --> 00:03:32.910
I just loved the fact
that he wrote me a letter.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.375
So, I called his parents
and I said, listen,

00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:39.480
you know, when a old guy picks
up your kid in a Italian car.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.453
- Yeah, yeah, that's not okay.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.393
- I said, your son wants me
to give him a ride to school.

00:03:42.393 --> 00:03:43.226
He's like, okay.

00:03:43.226 --> 00:03:44.760
- So, I go to the house, I pick him up.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.440
We pull up to the school,
you know, the Lamborghini's

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.540
got the doors that come up like this.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.650
He goes, bye, uncle Jay.

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:51.180
And I go, okay, I'll see you later.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.700
As I pull out, I hear a kid
go, he really is his uncle.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.186
Now I'm like, oh, what a liar I am.

00:03:55.186 --> 00:03:57.493
- Exactly, what did I just do?

00:03:57.493 --> 00:03:58.326
- Yeah, exactly.

00:03:58.326 --> 00:03:59.700
- You're a complicit.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.549
- I am complicit in
this child, yeah, yeah.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:03.382
- Yeah.

00:04:03.382 --> 00:04:04.410
- He's now in federal prison.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.670
I don't know what happened to the kid.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:06.729
- I'm sure!

00:04:06.729 --> 00:04:08.640
(Anna laughing)

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.670
- Speaking of lying, your
new show, Inventing Anna,

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:12.990
this is a true story, isn't it?

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:13.823
- Yes, this is a true story.

00:04:13.823 --> 00:04:15.585
- Because I remember this.

00:04:15.585 --> 00:04:18.150
- And then we fictionalized some of it.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.800
My character is a fictionalized version

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.190
of the author of the article
on which it is based.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.740
Jessica Pressler, but my
character's name is Vivian Kent.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.090
We fictionalized some other things,

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:29.580
but we're very honest about that,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.590
we say it right up front.
- Right, right.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:35.640
- But yes, most of it is
definitely based on fact,

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.523
based on everything that was
investigated in our article.

00:04:39.694 --> 00:04:40.527
The story about Anna Delvey.
- But what's the basis

00:04:40.527 --> 00:04:41.730
of the story, she pretends to be?

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.350
- She was a young, she
is still a young woman

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:50.100
who managed to scam her way all
the way to the top of, like,

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:55.100
New York society and really
get all of these perks,

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.900
and I'm the reporter who

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:58.747
investigates her story the whole way.

00:04:58.747 --> 00:05:01.320
- It's hard to believe
an attractive young woman

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.083
could scam men, I wonder how.

00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:03.916
(audience laughing)

00:05:03.916 --> 00:05:04.749
- You know.

00:05:04.749 --> 00:05:07.620
- It's so odd, it's an unusual story.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:10.350
- So, many people have seen
this program, so, you know,

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:13.560
and, so, I would suggest,
it's fun to watch it again

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:17.520
and imagine her as an older male.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.560
And it's not that confusing anymore

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.580
what she's doing to people.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:21.413
You know what I mean?
- Right, yeah, yeah.

00:05:21.413 --> 00:05:24.360
- It's like, oh, yeah, she
buys them things and then,

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.680
she buys them clothes and then tells them

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.440
that they look horrible in it, okay, yeah.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:29.910
He's trying to control you, right?

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.740
But it's like, because it comes from her,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.560
and she's young and she's personable,

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.880
it really did kind of cast a spell

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.897
on those for whom it was happening.

00:05:40.897 --> 00:05:42.780
- And she got away with
it for a long time, right?

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.890
- Yeah, and there's always
the question of, oh,

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:50.160
if she had just gotten her
funding for her startup,

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.600
would she have been called a
genius or called a scammer?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:55.433
- Right, right.

00:05:55.433 --> 00:05:58.350
- But, you know, yeah, you
gotta wonder those things.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:01.260
And the idea is, would she
just find the next con?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.310
You know, you never know.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.300
Because that's not how it turned out.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.800
- That's kind of like Elizabeth Holmes

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.510
or that Theranos deal.
- Right, it's really similar.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.400
- So many, because it was a young girl,

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.980
everybody wanted to believe, 19,

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.747
and let's give this kid a chance.

00:06:12.747 --> 00:06:14.280
- Yeah, yeah.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.710
And there's also that aspect of, like,

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:20.010
